From ea40afc051ffc32434d0ace7c974e6938122e866 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Cl=C3=A9ment=20Fiere?= <clement@fiere.fr>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 21:46:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(plugins): render a task menu action as a submenu

A plugin menu action could only ever be one selectable item, so a plugin
with a short list of frequent choices had nowhere to put them: the tags
plugin, for example, opens a modal to add one of the workspace's recent
tags, one menu open plus one modal plus one click per card.

TaskMenuActionRegistration.items(context) now turns an action into a
submenu: `label` becomes an unselectable trigger and the returned
TaskMenuSubItemRegistration[] are its children, in order, each run with
the same PluginTaskMenuContext. items() is synchronous and evaluated once
per menu build -- the host cannot await a menu item, so it reads cached
state.

run stays required and stays the flat behavior, which keeps one contract
for two host generations: a host predating `items` ignores the unknown
field and renders exactly the item it renders today, and an items() that
yields nothing usable (an empty list, or a throw -- caught, logged, and
treated as empty) falls back to the same flat item instead of producing a
trigger nothing can open. Nesting stops at this one level.

Rendering needs no new component: KanbanCardMenuEntry already models
"submenu" for the built-in Move to / Priority / Link menus, and both the
dropdown and context-menu renderers recurse into children, so cards, the
shared task-row menu, and the preview/detail menus all get it from the one
entry builder.
