 lists

`useTaskCommandChoices` rebuilt the sidebar/command-palette task commands
from `buildPrimaryPluginEntries` with `entry.kind === "item" && typeof
entry.label === "string"`, so an action that renders as a submenu was
silently dropped from that surface -- no trigger, no children, no
fallback, and with it this change would have removed an existing plugin
action (the tags plugin's "Add tag...") from the palette and from the
sidebar's task commands, which task-commands.test.tsx asserts are present.

`pluginCommandChoices` now walks the entry: a plugin submenu has no
activation of its own (no `onSelect`, an unselectable trigger), so its
item children become the commands, carrying their disabled flag and icon.
Nesting stops at the plugin's one allowed level, but the helper recurses
so a deeper tree degrades to its selectable leaves rather than vanishing.

Also corrects the `items` documentation: it is called while the host
builds a card's or row's menu entries, which happens on every render --
both the dropdown and the context variant, open or closed -- not "once per
open". It must stay cheap, synchronous and read-only, and an implementation
that scans or sorts should memoize on the state it reads.
