From dcb29b5eb598cab6872c4eb2e100e81ef153acd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Cl=C3=A9ment=20Fiere?= <clement@fiere.fr>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 22:21:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix(plugins): validate submenu children at the host
 boundary

`pluginSubItems` accepted whatever `items()` returned as long as it was a
non-empty array. A bundle is plain JavaScript, so the registration types
are not enforced at run time: `[null]` crashed the whole menu render while
building its icon and label, an entry without an id or label produced an
undefined label and a key React cannot distinguish, duplicate ids produced
duplicate keys, a child without a callable run failed only after the user
picked it, and an async callback (out of contract) left its rejection
unobserved, surfacing as an unhandled rejection out of the host's menu
build.

Children are now validated: `id` and `label` must be non-empty strings and
`run` must be a function, duplicate ids keep their first occurrence, and
unusable entries are dropped. A result with nothing usable left -- an
empty list, a throw, a promise, a non-array, or only invalid children --
falls back to the action's flat `run` item, which is what the docs already
promised. A promise is observed (never awaited) so its rejection cannot
escape. Each defect is logged once per action instead of on every menu
build, since `items()` runs on every render.

Also carries the icons doc note: task menu entries render a ready-made
element unchanged for plugins registered before icons were resolved that
way, while every other surface still maps an element to the fallback glyph
-- that shim is menu-only and deliberately not part of `PluginIcon`, since
widening the public type would promise a shape no other surface honours.

Command palette children now carry their trigger label as `context`, so a
bare tag name is identifiable in a listing of every task action.
